      "side": 1,
      "message": "While this causes a lot of gold diffs, almost all of them are with the Intel Iris having clear driver issues. Looking at the digest history, they have had flaky failures for a while and this is just changing and/or adding to them. At some point we need to track that down, but we aren\u0027t shipping on them yet in `grmtl`.\n\nIn other devices, the diffs are improvements where we go from MSAA quality to analytic quality because path rendering isn\u0027t used anymore.  The `zero_length_paths_aa` GMs are also improvements where comparing to device history, we are having two cells go from failing (red) to passing (green) whereas previously graphite (I believe any msaa config) would fail that entire row.\n\nThis shouldn\u0027t impact motionmark_lines performance as that was already going through drawPoints. But we\u0027ll see if anything else comes up in performance testing.",
      "revId": "908fde530a2a3de65f871ebde72a3ad1fa5cc274",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b4facd1e_328149d6",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Device.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 947,
