      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-14T18:48:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In Ganesh, Chris had chosen to send drawPath to the stroked tessellating path renderer when DMSAA was enabled as a priority so that they could be batched. In non-DMSAA it would get caught by the simplifications in GrStyledShape and be handled with a dedicated analytic op.\n\nGiven that we are trying to canonicalize the path to their base shape here already, I think it makes sense to include lines as a case, and we get the benefit of analytic coverage quality for lines. This is particularly nice for thin lines that might otherwise easily miss samples when only 4x is available.",
